{title: 531 - We'll Build on the Rock}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #531 • WELL BUILD ON THE ROCK • 9.8.9.7}
{lyricist: F. E. Belden}
{composer: F. E. Belden}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 531}
{meta: tune WELL BUILD ON THE ROCK}
{meta: meter 9.8.9.7}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Am/C]We’ll build on [G/D]the Rock, the living Rock,
[D7]On Jesus, the [G]Rock of Ages;
[D]So shall we abide [G]the fearful shock,
[G]When loud the tempest rages.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[G/B]We'll build [C]on the Rock,
[G]We'll build on the Rock;
[G]We'll build on the Rock, on the solid Rock,
[D]On Christ, the mighty Rock.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Am/C]Some build on [G/D]the sinking sands of life,
[D7]On visions of [G]earthly treasure;
[D]Some build on the waves [G]of sin and strife,
[G]Of fame, and worldly pleasure.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Am/C]O build on [G/D]the Rock, for ever sure,
[D7]The firm and the [G]true foundation;
[D]Its hope is the hope [G]which shall endure,
[G]The hope of our salvation.
{end_of_verse}
